## HTML Tables
A web table is an HTML structure which consists of multiple table rows with each row containing one or more table cells.
->Tables are block level elements.
->The size of the table is defined by the number of rows, cells and content.
<table> -> Defines table.
<tr>  -> Defines a row in a table.
<th>  -> Defines a header cell in a table.
<td>  -> Defines a cell in a table.


## What is an HTML Table?
HTML table is used to display data in rows and columns
Similar to an Excel spreadsheet
Tables are block-level elements

🔹 Basic Table Tags
<table> → Defines the table
<tr> → Defines a table row
<th> → Defines a header cell
Text is bold & centered
<td> → Defines a data cell
🔹 Table Structure
A table contains rows (<tr>)
Rows contain cells (<th> or <td>)
Table size depends on:
Number of rows
Number of columns
Content inside cells

🔹 Table Attributes
border → Adds border to table
colspan → Merges two or more columns
rowspan → Merges two or more rows
width → Sets table width (not recommended, use CSS)

🔹 Semantic Table Tags

<thead> → Table header section
<tbody> → Table body section
<tfoot> → Table footer section

